# Cross-platform reproducibility
#
# This repo is an installer that copies payload/ "byte for byte" into user repos.
# Without .gitattributes, Git for Windows defaults (core.autocrlf=true) check out
# payload/** with CRLF, which then ends up in the installed files, so Windows and
# macOS installs would differ (violating the "100% reproducible install" rule).
# npm pack/publish also packs from the working tree, so a Windows publish would ship CRLF.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF regardless of core.autocrlf.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: excluded from line-ending normalization
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.pyc binary
